From: liuqin Fedora maintainers <liuqin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: freeze userspace invocation waiters in place

Source: liuqin v0.7.0 9c741c403a4b07357d4ad2848fa0b1bc2f99927a
Adaptation: place the change in the local fastrpc_wait_for_completion()
helper instead of the call site; 7.3.1 already routes both paths there.
Rationale: the sensor daemon waits for an inbound DSP listener call. The
process freezer currently interrupts that wait, and the retried ioctl
sends a new context. TASK_FREEZABLE lets the waiter stop and resume
without resending the RPC; ordinary signals still interrupt.
Validation and rollback: tasks/upstream-refresh/RESULT.md.

---
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1326,7 +1326,9 @@
 		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ctx->work, 10 * HZ))
 			err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else {
-		err = wait_for_completion_interruptible(&ctx->work);
+		/* Retain the in-flight DSP context across system sleep. */
+		err = wait_for_completion_state(&ctx->work,
+					TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE);
 	}
 
 	return err;
